      "text": "your strength shall be spent in vain, Lev. 26:20. barrel of meal shall not waste, 1 Kgs. 17:14. Ye see … how Jerusalem lieth waste, Neh. 2:17. boar out of the wood doth waste it, Ps. 80:13. slothful … to him that is a great waster, Prov. 18:9. treasure … a foolish man spendeth it, Prov. 21:20. Until the cities be wasted without inhabitant, Isa. 6:11 (2 Ne. 16:11). Lord maketh the earth … waste, Isa. 24:1. generation to generation it shall lie waste, Isa. 34:10. I will make waste mountains, Isa. 42:15. created the waster to destroy, Isa. 54:16. do ye spend money for that which is not bread, Isa. 55:2. they shall build the old wastes, Isa. 61:4. our pleasant things are laid waste, Isa. 64:11. cities that are inhabited shall be laid waste, Ezek. 12:20. field is wasted, the land mourneth, Joel 1:10.",
